        "description": "Retained actual source inventory: two vertical plates with minus at the left and plus at the right, exactly six leftward field arrows, numbered point1 on the right and point2 on the left at the same field-line height, one open1-to2 curve bowed below the endpoints and one superposed orthogonal staircase. Retained author inventory records the lower source staircase/path ink as partly merged; the number of separately printed small legs and path-direction marks was not reliably established. The eight modern subdivisions and three directional marks are explicit uncalibrated regularization of that existing construction, not a claim about printed source counts, new data, another path or a particle-motion state. Native endpoint, signed-displacement and parallel/perpendicular assertions cover both numbered points and every staircase leg. No B/D, E-vector, distance or work/energy labels absent from fig139 are introduced. Sole native-marker repair lengthens the three existing curve-direction strokes along that same curve; their count and1-to2 direction are unchanged. This is a native readability/marker regularization, not a change to the source field, path endpoints or stair construction.",
